cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this release, please cite the paper and this archive."
title: "Blindboard v1: environment, harness, and evidence"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
# doi: add doi (the version DOI) and identifiers (the version and concept DOIs), as in the ClerkBench release.
authors:
  - family-names: Allcock
    given-names: Adam
    affiliation: Independent researcher
license:
  - CC-BY-4.0
  - Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/adamallcock/blindboard"
abstract: >-
  Code and data release for Blindboard, a benchmark that tests whether a
  language model can keep track of facts that keep changing: the symbol layout
  of a keyboard that is hidden and keeps being reshuffled. Includes the
  environment and its scripted reference solver, the harness that carries
  each model's reasoning between turns, every scored episode of both campaigns
  with full transcripts, the diagnostics behind every published number, and a
  one-command rebuild of every table and number in the paper.
keywords:
  - benchmark
  - large language models
  - state tracking
  - reasoning
  - evaluation
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: "Blindboard: Measuring State Tracking Under Interference with a Hidden, Shifting Keyboard"
  authors:
    - family-names: Allcock
      given-names: Adam
  year: 2026
